# Working in this provider

This is a Crossplane provider scaffolded by
[xp-provider-gen](https://github.com/cychiang/xp-provider-gen) in its **upjet**
flavor: your API types and controllers are generated from the
`{{ .TerraformProvider }}` Terraform provider's schema, not hand-written.

**Read [`docs/ownership.md`](docs/ownership.md) before editing anything.** It lists
which files you own and which the generator regenerates. It is itself generated,
so it is always accurate for this provider.

Three buckets, not two:
- Files whose top-of-file header marks them as generated by `xp-provider-gen`
  (registration, controller wiring, `main.go`, `config/provider.go`, and the rest
  of this generator's own plumbing) are tool-owned: `xp-provider-gen update`
  overwrites them.
- Everything upjet itself writes — every `zz_*.go` under `apis/**` and
  `internal/controller/**`, `config/zz_resources.go`, `package/crds/*.yaml`,
  `examples-generated/**` — is upjet's output, not yours: `make generate`
  overwrites it unconditionally every time it runs, whether or not you touched
  it, and it carries no header because it isn't this generator's template output
  at all.
- Everything else is yours forever, notably `config/<kind>/config.go` and
  `internal/clients/clients.go`.

