## Where your code goes

| You want to | Edit |
|---|---|
| Configure how a Terraform resource maps to its managed resource | `config/<kind>/config.go` |
| Map ProviderConfig credentials into the Terraform provider's config | `internal/clients/clients.go` |
| Add a resource kind | `xp-provider-gen create api --terraform-resource=...`, then `config/<kind>/config.go` |
| Provide a valid example / uptest input for a kind | `examples/<group>/<kind>.yaml` (see `test/README.md`) |
| Add a controller behavior test | `test/behavior/`, scaffolded by `xp-provider-gen create-test` once a kind has an example |

## After every `create api`

Run `make generate` to fetch the Terraform provider's schema and regenerate
types and controllers for the new resource. Nothing compiles until you do.

## Keeping up to date

`xp-provider-gen update` **refuses upjet projects**: its render path is
hard-wired to the native template set, not because anything is missing from
`PROJECT`. Pull in generator improvements by re-scaffolding or hand-porting
for now.

